title: 'Image: seed /dev/urandom at boot; rerun pentium2 gate after canlin entropy
  change'
updated: 2026-09-30T05:13:00Z
---

canlin now reads /dev/urandom for Mbed TLS entropy on musl (instead of the blocking /dev/random; found on a 3.4 kernel where TLS stalled). The i686 image should seed urandom at boot (saved seed on CANLINDATA, or equivalent) so early TLS is not predictable, and the qemu-system-i386 -cpu pentium2 gate should be re-run on the canlin runtime once it exists.
